{
  "id": "disengaged-family",
  "term": "disengaged family",
  "definition": "A disengaged family is a pattern of family dysfunction marked by overly separate or unbalanced boundaries between family members. In this kind of family system, the weak connectedness can contribute to poorer family communication and may be linked to worse perceived mental health.",
